WEBVTT

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.490
Previously on Smallville.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.490
What's with the wardrobe malfunction?

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.490
What?

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:07.490
Where are you going all dressed up?

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.490
When a guy likes a girl?

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.490
He asks her out.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.490
I'm a true believer in this red and blue super dude.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.490
Hello.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.489
Can I count on you to publish that letter from the guy.

00:00:17.489 --> 00:00:19.489
I have to see you.

00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:20.489
How do you feel about phone booths?

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:22.489
Let's say midnight.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.489
Test Mercer, acting CEO of Luthercle.

00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:27.489
You're my boss?

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:30.489
Mark, if you don't want to admit your true identity, that's fine.

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:34.490
that's fine. But we both know that Davis Bloom isn't a man. He's a beast.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:42.070
Lex knew that orb wasn't from this earth.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:46.070
There's life inside it that can't be released until the traveler kills the beast.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.070
Use the ring. Send doomsday to the future.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:56.329
Oliver crossed the line. He killed Lex Luthor.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:59.329
You're making a big mistake. You're not one of us anymore.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:04.329
David Clark can't buttoned up in a starch shirt and tie,

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:06.329
but then when he's playing the hero...

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:07.329
That's out of his red and blue?

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:10.329
It was red and blue, creating two completely separate identities.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:13.900
I love you.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.900
Henry James Olson.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.900
Rest in peace.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:19.900
Jimmy wanted to know that no matter where I was in the city,

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.900
I could look up here and see this beacon, the watchtown.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.900
I'm the reason Jimmy's dead.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.900
What are you saying?

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.900
Goodbye, Croy.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.900
Clark Kent is dead.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.900
And now, the season premiere of Smallville.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:45.180
Lois Lane.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.180
My cousin has been missing for three weeks.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:50.260
Yes.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.260
I'm the same woman who called yesterday and the day before that and pretty much every day for the last few weeks

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.260
because I have not been getting any answers to my question.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:02.780
You know, don't worry about the second cursor on your screen.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.780
I just hacked into your system because you have been so completely unhelpful that I can't...

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:36.800
I wouldn't come any further unless you're interested in an impromptu nose job.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.659
Dr. Hamilton.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:47.659
If you would be so kind as to lower the 9mm Jericho 941, I prefer a meal.

00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:49.659
I'm sorry I didn't even scare you.

00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:50.659
I've just...

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:53.659
I've just been haunted by my own share of ghosts lately.

00:02:53.659 --> 00:02:54.659
And the gun?

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:56.659
After everything that's happened to being here alone,

00:02:56.659 --> 00:02:58.659
it's the only way I can sleep.

00:02:58.659 --> 00:02:59.659
Did Ollie send you?

00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:01.659
I've been calling him nonstop lately.

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:02.659
I know.

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:04.659
I think you can stop calling.

00:03:04.659 --> 00:03:07.659
Obviously, he's not gonna answer.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:08.659
They're gone, Chloe.

00:03:08.659 --> 00:03:09.659
All of them.

00:03:09.659 --> 00:03:10.659
They're not gone.

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:12.659
Ollie, Dinah, Bart.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.659
They're just vanished off the grid, but they're not...

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:15.659
They don't want to be found.

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:18.659
Jimmy died because they turned on each other

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:19.659
and now they have to live with that guilt.

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:20.659
I'm sure that you.

00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:22.659
Jimmy's death is haunting Clark every day,

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:24.659
but he still does everything he can

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:26.659
to make sure that the streets of Metropolis are still protected.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:28.659
And he seems to be doing an adequate job

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:30.659
without his sidekick.

00:03:30.659 --> 00:07:35.019
When you decided to return to your training,

00:07:35.019 --> 00:07:37.019
I assumed you were ready.

00:07:37.019 --> 00:07:39.019
I've been coming here for weeks.

00:07:39.019 --> 00:07:41.019
I've done everything you asked.

00:07:41.019 --> 00:07:43.019
Why are you questioning me now?

00:07:43.019 --> 00:07:45.019
Until today, you had focus.

00:07:45.019 --> 00:07:48.019
You had cleared your mind and heart

00:07:48.019 --> 00:07:51.019
of those who had kept you tethered to the human realm.

00:07:51.019 --> 00:07:54.019
If there's anything that's keeping me tethered,

00:07:54.019 --> 00:07:56.019
it's that I still can't fly.

00:07:56.019 --> 00:08:00.009
Have I not earned the same powers that Kara has?

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:02.009
Your powers lie within you, Carlisle.

00:08:02.009 --> 00:08:06.009
Your physical composition is no different than your cousins.

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:10.120
You're saying it's all in my head?

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:13.120
You still see yourself as a human.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.850
You're wrong.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.850
I gave up everyone I cared about.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.850
I gave up everyone who was important to me.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:26.850
I were the symbol of our family every day to remind me that I have a different

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.850
destiny. Perhaps you've tried to move on too quickly.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:35.850
The test of a true hero is to struggle with feelings of loss and to overcome them,

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:38.850
not to avoid them.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.850
Something or someone is holding you back.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:48.450
No. I've come this far and I'm not looking back.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.450
I can do this.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:57.200
The desk nurse

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.110
called me. Where have you been? What happened to you?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.110
Um, Tess was rambling about some alien orb,

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.110
and then we threw down in the middle of the Daily Planet,

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:20.110
and wham, I wake up in a monorail car with some ninja chick after me.

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:22.110
Alien orb? Lowe.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.110
I think maybe you just bumped your head in the accident.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:28.110
Wait, where have I been?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:32.110
You were the one who was playing Phelma and Louise with a creature from the Black Lagoon.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.110
How did you manage to ditch Davis?

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.110
I didn't exactly ditch Davis.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.110
I didn't exactly ditch Davis.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:42.110
Lowe, it was the red-blue blur, wasn't it?

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:48.440
He promised me he'd save you, and he did.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.720
That means he's still alive.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.720
The train.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.720
He saved the train, too, didn't he?

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.720
You've been talking to the blur?

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.720
Yes, he sort of confides in me.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.720
Of course he does.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:11.340
Holy, it's almost midnight. I promised I'd meet him. I'm gonna be late.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.340
Lois, you are way beyond late, okay?

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.340
You just need to slow down.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.340
There's something that you need to.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.340
to know.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:20.340
He is the only one who can help me escape from the jaws of crouching tigers.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.340
I'm sorry, Chloe.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.340
Whatever it is, it's gonna have to wait.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:24.340
No, Lois, you need to wait.

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:25.340
Okay?

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:28.340
I've got kind of a big bomb I need to drop on you.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:33.620
You know what?

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.620
You're right.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.620
I...

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:39.620
I probably just took one on the noggin, and now I'm flipping out.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.620
I think I could use a sedative.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.620
It's been kind of a long day.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.620
I'll get you too.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:11:24.580
Look, I know what she did for Chloe.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.580
At least let me thank you.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:32.990
Look.

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.490
I'm sorry, I'm late.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:38.570
Promise you can trust me.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:42.259
Please.

00:11:42.259 --> 00:11:45.799
I know you're out there somewhere.

00:11:45.799 --> 00:12:28.000
Have you had time to move beyond these mental trials?

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Your determination is strong, myself.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:34.000
But just as your passion will be your greatest strength,

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.000
so too will it be your greatest obstacle.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.200
Jimmy died because of me

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:45.679
and I can't afford to let another mistake like that happen.

00:12:45.679 --> 00:12:50.399
You sent me here to fulfill a destiny.

00:12:50.399 --> 00:12:53.649
Tell me what you need for me.

00:12:53.649 --> 00:12:54.649
Carlisle, you do not need for me.

00:12:54.649 --> 00:12:57.649
Do not need me to tell you what is standing in your way.

00:12:57.649 --> 00:13:04.440
You already know, and you know what you need to do.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.440
I have to say goodbye to her.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:27.259
I lost their trail.

00:13:27.259 --> 00:13:39.279
There must be more of us out there.

00:13:39.279 --> 00:13:45.509
What about the woman? Has she spoken yet?

00:13:45.509 --> 00:13:46.509
No, sir.

00:13:46.509 --> 00:13:54.679
Permission to speak freely.

00:13:54.679 --> 00:13:57.679
Major, the woman isn't an ally.

00:13:57.679 --> 00:14:06.210
She's hiding something.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:07.210
And you think I am, too.

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.210
Why don't we have the powers we should have under Yellow Sun?

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:18.110
My authority has been questioned by two budding cadets.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.110
We deserve to know what happened to us.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:21.110
How did we get here?

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.110
There is enough.

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:24.110
Does anybody know we're here?

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:27.059
Salute.

00:14:27.059 --> 00:14:30.139
Neil.

00:14:30.139 --> 00:14:35.399
Hill before Zard.

00:14:35.399 --> 00:14:48.610
Oliver, I don't know where you've disappeared to you,

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.610
but I'm already low on one superhero today.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:55.610
Chloe thinks I'm crazy, and I'm low on clues as to why some she-nidgen is after me.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:15:05.000
Call me.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.000
Good find?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:12.330
Look, on a scale of one to ten of illegal things I've done in my life,

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.330
this doesn't even hit the radar.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:17.350
Okay, that didn't exactly come out right.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.350
All I'm saying is you and your big boys in blue

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.350
have bigger fish to fry than this little guppy,

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.350
so I'm just going to...

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:26.200
How about a name?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.200
Lois Lane, Daily Planet.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.450
Lane?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.450
You're the report that's been missing for three weeks?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.450
Missing?

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.700
What the hell are you talking about?

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:40.700
What day is it?

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.700
It's Friday. The 25th?

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:55.309
What? Where the hell have I been for three weeks?

00:15:55.309 --> 00:15:57.309
I was kind of hoping you'd tell me.

00:15:57.309 --> 00:15:58.309
You tell me.

00:15:58.309 --> 00:16:02.309
You're M-I-A until your name came up on the list of crash victims.

00:16:02.309 --> 00:16:08.549
Now, do you remember anything last night that would explain how a seven-ton sky train belly-flops

00:16:08.549 --> 00:16:12.309
onto Main Street without a single fatality?

00:16:12.309 --> 00:16:22.340
Guess we just need to chalk it up to a modern-day miracle.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:27.840
We could, or we could chalk it up to a vigilante on an ego trip.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:34.009
Oh, is that what we call courage these days?

00:16:34.009 --> 00:16:35.009
Infamous blur.

00:16:35.009 --> 00:16:36.009
You know, the end.

00:16:36.009 --> 00:16:38.009
The sins don't always justify the means.

00:16:38.009 --> 00:16:41.009
You might want to stick to your night job, detective.

00:16:41.009 --> 00:16:44.009
Graffiti's not exactly the red-blue blur style.

00:16:44.009 --> 00:16:46.009
You're right.

00:16:46.009 --> 00:16:47.009
Never used to be.

00:16:47.009 --> 00:16:50.009
Back when the guy was happy pulling off a few modest saves,

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:53.009
but then suddenly there was no red or blue.

00:16:53.009 --> 00:16:55.009
It was just the blur.

00:16:55.009 --> 00:16:57.009
Now he feels the need to leave his mark

00:16:57.009 --> 00:17:01.009
all over the city to, I don't know, prove something.

00:17:01.009 --> 00:17:04.009
Great. The rest of your posse to interrogate me...

00:17:04.009 --> 00:17:10.049
To want membership in the mile-long club,

00:17:10.049 --> 00:17:12.049
you might want to try one that's stolen traps.

00:17:12.049 --> 00:17:14.049
So get out of here.

00:17:14.049 --> 00:17:16.049
Okay, officer.

00:17:16.049 --> 00:17:18.460
Not bad.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:18:01.160
Oliver may be AWOL, but his funds aren't.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.160
Shouldn't you be mothballing a lab

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.160
or packing up Oliver's plether collection?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.160
You made a solid argument earlier.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:14.160
Sometimes we tried to forget, but there are things,

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.160
well, there are people.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.160
are people worth fighting for.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:22.539
I don't know what to say.

00:18:22.539 --> 00:18:27.400
I'd be more comfortable if we just got down to work.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:30.400
Okay.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.400
My cousin Lois vanished for three weeks,

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:35.400
and then suddenly appeared claiming that she was being chased

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.400
by a ninja-clad assassin.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.400
Where was she?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.400
That she has no memory of,

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:43.400
but luckily she did leave a souvenir from her trip.

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:46.400
Now I know this may sound crazy to you,

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:51.839
but I think I know where she was, the future.

00:18:51.839 --> 00:18:54.839
Transversing chronal anomalies.

00:18:54.839 --> 00:19:01.200
I ran some scans at the time of the monorail crash

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:07.200
and discovered two rips in the temporal aperture continuum.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:16.490
Okay, I've never actually said this before, but could you dumb that down just a little bit?

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.490
Two rips in the fabric of our universe.

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:22.490
Okay, well Lois explains one of them, but the other...

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:30.519
Maybe she's not delusional.

00:19:30.519 --> 00:19:32.519
Maybe somebody came back from the future with her.

00:19:32.519 --> 00:19:33.519
future with her.

00:19:33.519 --> 00:20:17.980
Who the hell are you?

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:18.980
Major Zod.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:24.680
I don't understand.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.680
They talked about you like you were their leader.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.680
Before they lost their faith.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:39.440
I ordered them to find out what you know about the circumstances surrounding our arrival.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:47.690
They weren't successful. They took the wrong approach with you.

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:52.690
Let's leave the getting to know you part for later.

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:56.690
It's obvious you've become accustomed to abuse over the year.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:20:59.690
It only triggers an obstinate reaction.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:03.690
A more emotional approach would have been my preference.

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:10.960
Vulnerability.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:18.470
You're not the same voice as the orb.

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:22.160
Who was that?

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:29.799
Oh, you don't know, do you?

00:21:29.799 --> 00:21:34.259
And you expect me to fill in the missing pieces?

00:21:34.259 --> 00:21:38.309
I have no expectations of you.

00:21:38.309 --> 00:21:50.160
I was told that you would come here and save this planet from its own destruction.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:53.509
That you'd have certain abilities.

00:21:53.509 --> 00:21:59.289
But you don't even know what you're doing here.

00:21:59.289 --> 00:22:03.470
Do you?

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:04.470
They think you're holding out.

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:10.680
But when they find that you're just as confused as they are,

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.680
they won't need you.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:22.099
I think if we work together,

00:22:22.099 --> 00:22:25.099
we can get past the guard.

00:22:25.099 --> 00:22:27.099
Escape.

00:22:27.099 --> 00:22:29.099
You'll be shot before you reach the yard.

00:22:29.099 --> 00:22:34.269
After the last few days,

00:22:34.269 --> 00:22:43.380
it'd be a blessing to be shot to death.

00:22:43.380 --> 00:22:45.380
I never said that'd kill you.

00:22:45.380 --> 00:23:00.319
I, on the other hand, will not hesitate.

00:23:00.319 --> 00:23:21.289
For three weeks, I've been trying to track you down

00:23:21.289 --> 00:23:23.289
and you're completely off the radar.

00:23:23.289 --> 00:23:24.289
Lois shows up for one.

00:23:24.289 --> 00:23:26.289
one day and you're as predictable as clockwork.

00:23:26.289 --> 00:23:35.500
It wasn't that I didn't want to come by and see that you were okay.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:37.940
I know.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:42.950
Leaving everyone behind.

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:47.190
It's not what I wanted.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.190
It isn't about what we want, Clark.

00:23:49.190 --> 00:23:51.190
It's about what the rest of the world needs.

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:53.190
I get it.

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:55.190
I was lucky to be a part of your life for a little while,

00:23:55.190 --> 00:24:00.630
but we both know that you'd have to move on one day.

00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:05.960
I started the training Jerell always planned for me.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.960
Everything that I've learned and he showed me.

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:09.960
My old life seems very far away.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:10.960
My old life seems very far away.

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:15.210
You're doing the right thing, Clark.

00:24:15.210 --> 00:24:17.210
You can't look back.

00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:19.210
It's the only way I can stay focused.

00:24:19.210 --> 00:24:24.549
Stay objective.

00:24:24.549 --> 00:24:26.549
But letting go everyone that I care about.

00:24:26.549 --> 00:24:29.549
I'm cutting every attachment that may influence the choices that I have to make.

00:24:29.549 --> 00:24:36.180
So what part of that involves skoking around a phone booth looking for Lois?

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:41.380
It's not like that.

00:24:41.380 --> 00:24:44.380
Yes, I came back to find her, but only say goodbye.

00:24:44.380 --> 00:24:46.380
Well, let's hope you still have a chance.

00:24:46.380 --> 00:24:50.170
I think Lois found your lucky charm and hitchhiking.

00:24:50.170 --> 00:24:52.170
and hitchhike to the future.

00:24:52.170 --> 00:24:55.000
Is she?

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:56.000
She's fine.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:59.000
She doesn't remember anything, but she didn't come back alone.

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:02.000
And it looks like her excess baggage might be trying to kill her.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:44.839
Oh, legs?

00:25:44.839 --> 00:25:47.839
Legs, really? Is that a good idea?

00:25:47.839 --> 00:25:49.839
You're drunk.

00:25:49.839 --> 00:25:51.839
What are you doing here? Where are you been?

00:25:51.839 --> 00:25:53.839
Didn't you get my messages?

00:25:53.839 --> 00:25:56.839
Yeah, my phone's been kind of MIA for a while now.

00:25:56.839 --> 00:25:58.839
How'd you find me?

00:25:58.839 --> 00:26:01.839
It wasn't that difficult to track down the tabloid.

00:26:01.839 --> 00:26:04.839
Prince of Metropolis, I just had to follow the paparazzi.

00:26:04.839 --> 00:26:09.839
But your little, uh, lame, sexist boy club wouldn't let me in, so I had to improvise.

00:26:09.839 --> 00:26:12.839
Oh, you poor Warren, you low, so I'm not having my best around here.

00:26:12.839 --> 00:26:14.839
This guy.

00:26:14.839 --> 00:26:15.839
I noticed.

00:26:15.839 --> 00:26:18.839
Look, you may be on some Death Wish fast track,

00:26:18.839 --> 00:26:22.839
but I could really use a little dose of hero about now.

00:26:22.839 --> 00:26:24.839
Hey, lady.

00:26:24.839 --> 00:26:26.839
Listen to me.

00:26:26.839 --> 00:26:31.779
I blacked out three weeks ago, turn up in a monorail car that's jumped off the tracks, and now some

00:26:31.839 --> 00:26:33.839
assassin woman is after me.

00:26:33.839 --> 00:26:55.359
Can you repeat that?

00:26:55.359 --> 00:26:57.359
I knew you'd be watching her.

00:26:57.359 --> 00:26:59.359
I was never after Lois.

00:26:59.359 --> 00:27:01.359
I want you.

00:27:01.359 --> 00:27:21.789
Your future to come after me. Why?

00:27:21.789 --> 00:27:23.789
Because you betrayed us.

00:27:23.789 --> 00:27:30.240
My father's watch.

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:42.230
The date is set one year in the future.

00:27:42.230 --> 00:27:45.369
How'd you get this?

00:27:45.369 --> 00:27:47.369
You gave it to me.

00:27:47.369 --> 00:27:56.180
How do you know about it?

00:27:56.180 --> 00:27:59.180
Blue kryptonite takes away my abilities too.

00:27:59.180 --> 00:28:04.740
We're of the same world, Callow.

00:28:04.740 --> 00:28:05.740
Why are you risking your alone?

00:28:05.740 --> 00:28:11.740
Because it's the only chance I have to defeat you before you destroy our world.

00:28:11.740 --> 00:29:46.180
I'm disappointed.

00:29:46.180 --> 00:29:49.180
There you go. So you sound like every other ex-girlfriend I ever had.

00:29:49.180 --> 00:29:52.180
Yes, but I'm not like every other ex you've had.

00:29:52.180 --> 00:29:55.180
You're not. Can't seem to get you back in my bed.

00:29:55.180 --> 00:29:59.180
Look, you know what? You can't fool me.

00:29:59.180 --> 00:30:02.180
You risk your life to help strangers.

00:30:02.180 --> 00:30:06.180
So you can plaster with that frat boy ground across your face.

00:30:06.180 --> 00:30:09.180
But I know that you are real here.

00:30:09.180 --> 00:30:10.180
on to me.

00:30:10.180 --> 00:30:14.769
Look, Lois, when are you going to learn?

00:30:14.769 --> 00:30:15.769
Okay?

00:30:15.769 --> 00:30:17.769
I'm nothing more than a shallow playboy.

00:30:17.769 --> 00:30:19.769
I got the tabloid covers to prove it.

00:30:19.769 --> 00:30:24.819
Then how do you explain the whole Green Arrow thing?

00:30:24.819 --> 00:30:27.819
You know, the hero thing kind of distracting me for a little while.

00:30:27.819 --> 00:30:28.819
So did you.

00:30:28.819 --> 00:30:35.339
You're an obnoxious jackass.

00:30:35.339 --> 00:30:38.579
There you go, see?

00:30:38.579 --> 00:30:40.579
Now you finally starting to catch on.

00:30:40.579 --> 00:30:48.680
Look, I'm sorry if you ever thought I was anything more than that, Lois, but it's not my fault.

00:30:48.680 --> 00:30:56.529
You know what, that's okay.

00:30:56.529 --> 00:30:57.529
Really?

00:30:57.529 --> 00:30:58.529
I guess you know yourself better than anyone, right?

00:30:58.529 --> 00:30:59.529
than anyone, right?

00:30:59.529 --> 00:31:05.650
You know what?

00:31:05.650 --> 00:31:07.650
Maybe I don't really need you, Ollie.

00:31:07.650 --> 00:31:09.650
I've already found my real hero.

00:31:09.650 --> 00:31:34.190
What juncture did you join forces with Major Zod?

00:31:34.190 --> 00:31:37.190
I never met the Major, until today.

00:31:37.190 --> 00:31:39.190
What about the others?

00:31:39.190 --> 00:31:41.190
There should be hundreds of us, we've only found dozens.

00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:42.190
Where are they?

00:31:42.190 --> 00:31:44.190
I was taking orders.

00:31:44.190 --> 00:31:47.190
Just like all of you.

00:31:47.190 --> 00:31:50.190
I thought that I was saving your civilization.

00:31:50.190 --> 00:31:53.190
Do you really think that a civilian,

00:31:53.190 --> 00:31:54.190
with no super abilities,

00:31:54.190 --> 00:31:59.190
would team up with one man instead of an entire army?

00:31:59.190 --> 00:32:04.190
If you want answers, why don't you try asking the one man who has left you in the dark

00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:06.190
this entire time?

00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:09.190
Impressive.

00:32:09.190 --> 00:32:15.190
Major, the last thing we remember is our blood being taken in camp before the battle in Kandor.

00:32:15.190 --> 00:32:17.190
How did we get here?

00:32:17.190 --> 00:32:21.470
If we're here, there can only be one explanation.

00:32:21.470 --> 00:32:24.970
Our home has been destroyed.

00:32:24.970 --> 00:32:28.339
You've taken it upon yourself to betray.

00:32:28.339 --> 00:32:31.940
upon yourself to betray us?

00:32:31.940 --> 00:32:32.940
Have you killed the others?

00:32:32.940 --> 00:32:33.940
What happened to our power?

00:32:33.940 --> 00:32:41.670
You dare defy me.

00:32:41.670 --> 00:32:49.289
I have saved the lives of half of the soldiers in this room.

00:32:49.289 --> 00:32:52.289
You know I have risked more than any of you.

00:32:52.289 --> 00:33:03.920
Not one of you has sacrificed what I have for our survival.

00:33:03.920 --> 00:33:13.279
Do you want a leader who hides away in his mansion for weeks on end and complaints?

00:33:13.279 --> 00:33:18.279
Or do you want a leader who ventured out, alone, scouring a hostile,

00:33:18.279 --> 00:33:20.279
in search of your loved ones.

00:33:20.279 --> 00:33:27.500
I have always been true to my word,

00:33:27.500 --> 00:33:32.230
and I will find the answers we are looking for,

00:33:32.230 --> 00:33:35.230
or I will die in the quest.

00:33:35.230 --> 00:34:31.969
It's over.

00:34:31.969 --> 00:34:35.349
Who was she?

00:34:35.349 --> 00:34:36.349
I don't know.

00:34:36.349 --> 00:34:38.349
I have a feeling I'm going to find out.

00:34:38.349 --> 00:34:40.349
She's some krypton.

00:34:40.349 --> 00:34:41.349
Crypton?

00:34:41.349 --> 00:34:42.349
Crypton?

00:34:42.349 --> 00:34:43.349
I don't understand.

00:34:43.349 --> 00:34:45.349
What was she doing here?

00:34:45.349 --> 00:34:46.349
What did she say?

00:34:46.349 --> 00:34:49.349
She told me that I would cause the end of the world.

00:34:49.349 --> 00:34:50.349
It's like I have ever.

00:34:50.349 --> 00:34:52.349
It's like I have a ticking bomb on me, Chloe,

00:34:52.349 --> 00:34:56.719
and I only have a year to figure out how to stop it.

00:34:56.719 --> 00:34:59.719
Well, you can't believe everything in assassin tells you.

00:34:59.719 --> 00:35:04.090
I mean, what does she know anyway, right?

00:35:04.090 --> 00:35:05.090
The future.

00:35:05.090 --> 00:35:11.280
Right.

00:35:11.280 --> 00:35:13.280
The future.

00:35:13.280 --> 00:35:26.760
What is it, Chloe?

00:35:26.760 --> 00:35:28.760
I want you to go back and save Jimmy.

00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:35.219
Take the ring and stop him from being killed.

00:35:35.219 --> 00:35:36.219
You can't ask me to...

00:35:36.219 --> 00:35:37.219
Clark.

00:35:37.219 --> 00:35:40.219
You said that your sole purpose for giving everything up

00:35:40.219 --> 00:35:43.219
is so that you could dedicate your life to helping people.

00:35:43.219 --> 00:35:44.219
So how you could dedicate your life to helping people.

00:35:44.219 --> 00:35:46.219
So help him. Clark save him.

00:35:46.219 --> 00:35:51.260
That would be changing destiny.

00:35:51.260 --> 00:35:54.260
Whose destiny? Not Jimmy's. You and I both know that.

00:35:54.260 --> 00:35:56.260
He didn't deserve to die, Clark.

00:35:56.260 --> 00:35:58.260
He died because you and I screwed up.

00:35:58.260 --> 00:36:00.260
Because we made a mistake. Now you have to fix it.

00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:02.260
I'm not a god.

00:36:02.260 --> 00:36:06.260
And the last time that I tried to rewrite fate, my own father died.

00:36:06.260 --> 00:36:10.440
He died right here in my arms because of me.

00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:23.320
I've given him so much for you, Clark.

00:36:23.320 --> 00:36:29.139
This is the only thing I've ever asked for you.

00:36:29.139 --> 00:36:35.590
Please do this for me. Please save Jimmy.

00:36:35.590 --> 00:36:47.760
It's good.

00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:52.639
It's good that you're embracing your Kryptonian side.

00:36:52.639 --> 00:37:01.050
There isn't really anything human left in you.

00:37:01.050 --> 00:37:28.909
Miss Mercer.

00:37:28.909 --> 00:37:30.909
How are you feeling?

00:37:30.909 --> 00:37:33.909
Well, you should know you had a front row ticket to the entire thing.

00:37:33.909 --> 00:37:36.909
How the hell can they just disappear?

00:37:36.909 --> 00:37:40.539
Where's my video?

00:37:40.539 --> 00:37:42.539
You told us not to interfere under any circumstance

00:37:42.539 --> 00:37:44.539
when they came in and took you hostage.

00:37:44.539 --> 00:37:46.539
And I'm sure that you enjoyed every moment of it.

00:37:46.539 --> 00:37:48.539
Just tell me that my plan paid off.

00:37:48.539 --> 00:37:50.539
Where are they?

00:37:50.539 --> 00:37:51.539
We recorded hundreds of hours.

00:37:51.539 --> 00:37:54.539
recorded hundreds of hours of security footage while they were here.

00:37:54.539 --> 00:37:57.539
I've only been able to sift through some of...

00:37:57.539 --> 00:37:58.539
...feeds.

00:37:58.539 --> 00:38:05.360
It's all gone. There's not even a trace of the video feed files.

00:38:05.360 --> 00:38:11.000
They broke through a high security software.

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:19.750
I guess a few encrypted passwords won't stop someone who traveled galaxies to get here.

00:38:19.750 --> 00:38:34.699
Clark?

00:38:34.699 --> 00:38:41.530
There are laws about stalking people.

00:38:41.530 --> 00:38:43.530
You should know.

00:38:43.530 --> 00:38:46.530
Hmm. I'm not a cop.

00:38:46.530 --> 00:38:49.530
Detective, whatever. You guys are so touchy.

00:38:49.530 --> 00:38:51.530
I don't work for the force.

00:38:51.530 --> 00:38:54.530
You jump to that conclusion yourself, which I hear you do.

00:38:54.530 --> 00:38:56.530
A lot.

00:38:56.530 --> 00:39:00.960
Who the hell are you, then?

00:39:00.960 --> 00:39:03.960
I'm a field reporter.

00:39:03.960 --> 00:39:06.960
I spent the last few years in Afghanistan.

00:39:06.960 --> 00:39:09.960
Hopefully that gave me enough training to be your deskmate.

00:39:09.960 --> 00:39:12.960
Don't bet on it.

00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:15.960
And don't get comfortable in that chair. Clark's coming back.

00:39:15.960 --> 00:39:17.960
Really?

00:39:17.960 --> 00:39:20.960
I already was visiting family indefinitely.

00:39:20.960 --> 00:39:21.960
Indefinitely.

00:39:21.960 --> 00:39:23.960
No.

00:39:23.960 --> 00:39:25.960
The guy never takes any time off.

00:39:25.960 --> 00:39:28.960
I'm sure he's just cashing in on some overdue vacation time.

00:39:28.960 --> 00:39:29.960
Oh.

00:39:29.960 --> 00:39:33.309
Supposedly you've been fired.

00:39:33.309 --> 00:39:36.590
Minor technicality.

00:39:36.590 --> 00:39:37.590
I hope so.

00:39:37.590 --> 00:39:50.480
I'm John Corbyn. I'll see you in the trenches.

00:39:50.480 --> 00:40:18.909
Okay.

00:40:18.909 --> 00:40:19.909
Hello.

00:40:19.909 --> 00:40:24.559
Lois.

00:40:24.559 --> 00:40:26.559
Thank you for saving me out there.

00:40:26.559 --> 00:40:28.559
I was afraid you had disappeared for good.

00:40:28.559 --> 00:40:30.559
I should have.

00:40:30.559 --> 00:40:40.789
I'm supposed to.

00:40:40.789 --> 00:40:41.789
Promise me this is just just.

00:40:41.789 --> 00:40:42.789
Just between us?

